## Concerns and blockers

- **No production blocker remains for the provider-free proof.**
- The tracked existing pytest node is stale and remains red for the schema-v2 fixture/API drift described above. It was intentionally not edited.
- On this Windows host, the successful proof needed compact ignored evidence path names to stay below legacy path limits and needed execution outside the filesystem sandbox so production's secure Win32 directory handles could reopen mode-0700 audit directories. These are local harness-environment constraints, not provider or optimizer-loop failures.
- Failed harness-only evidence is retained, ignored, and superseded by `proof-g`: `proof-20260829-b`, `proof-20260829-c`, `proof-20260829-d`, `proof-20260829-e`, and `proof-f`. The `proof-20260829-c`, `proof-20260829-d`, and `proof-20260829-e` roots contain production audit subdirectories whose secure ACLs deny ordinary sandbox traversal; `proof-g` deliberately retains the same protection on successful durable evidence. These evidence roots are not ephemeral controller/source roots or live processes.
- There are no remaining `t5c-*`, `t5s-*`, or `task5-*` OS-temp targets. The one failed-run root previously created at `C:/Users/llong/AppData/Local/Temp/task5-available_pricing-controller-d3um9x13` was removed by exact literal path and independently verified absent.
- No live provider or pricing service was contacted. No real performance, return, trading, or investability conclusion can be drawn from the simulated discovery winner.

